<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">I saw three ships come sailing by on New Year's Day</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">19th century</span><span class="sg-chain-h">version with three girls and a New Year's Day wedding</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Bells of Heaven (sung by Elizabeth Cronin)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1952</span><span class="sg-chain-h">Irish traditional version</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">I Saw Three Ships (arr. Martin Shaw, The Oxford Book of Carols)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">arrangement</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">I Saw Three Ships (arr. David Willcocks, Carols for Choirs)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">arrangement</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">I Saw Three Ships (arr. John Rutter, Carols for Choirs)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">arrangement</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Carols of All Seasons (Jean Ritchie)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1959</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording of her family's version</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Magic of Christmas (Nat King Cole)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1960</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">3 Ships (Jon Anderson)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1985</span><span class="sg-chain-h">title track</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Christmas Album (Keith Emerson)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1988</span><span class="sg-chain-h">instrumental rock adaptation</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">A Very Special Christmas 3 (Sting)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1997</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Caroline, or Change (musical)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">used as a counterpoint</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired-by"><h2>What it drew on</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">As I Sat On a Sunny Bank</span><span class="sg-chain-h">probably the song's traditional name and form</span></li></ul></section>
